// @contract: C-197
// The prim allocators (`prim.alloc_list` / `alloc_list_f64` / `alloc_bytes` /
// `alloc_str`, the self-host's floor) judge their element count in i64 BEFORE
// the i32 wrap — the `bytes.new` / `bytes.repeat` rule. A count past the
// structural bound is the defined `Error: out of memory` abort on both legs.
// Before, `read_f16_le_array(b, 0, i64::MAX)` wrapped `n * 8` to a small size
// the allocator satisfied, and the first element store past it was a raw
// out-of-bounds trap (exit 134) against native's C-197 abort (exit 1) —
// differential fuzz, seed 542118604760 index 417.
fn main() -> Unit = {
  println("before")
  let xs = bytes.read_f16_le_array(bytes.from_list([255, 123, 0, 60]), 0, 9223372036854775807)
  println("unreachable ${list.len(xs)}")
}
